<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Arab Kingdom of Syria</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1920 CE · capital Damascus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Arab kingdom, proclaimed in Damascus under Faisal in 1920 and destroyed by France within months.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Faisal, son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharif-of-mecca">Sharif of Mecca</a>, entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> in October 1918 with the Arab army of the revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and set up a government under the British-led <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/occupied-enemy-territory-administration">Occupied Enemy Territory Administration</a>. On 8 March 1920 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrian-national-congress">Syrian National Congress</a> proclaimed him king of an independent <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> including <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lebanese-republic">Lebanon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government drew on Arab nationalist officers and notables, many of them former Ottoman officials. The Congress drafted a constitution for a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hashim-al-atassi">Hashim al-Atassi</a> as prime minister. The state's control was limited to the inland cities, and its finances depended on British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subsidy">subsidies</a> that ended in 1919.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-remo-conference">San Remo conference</a> gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> the mandate for <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> in April 1920. France sent an ultimatum, and on 24 July 1920 its army defeated the Syrian force at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maysalun">Maysalun</a>, where the war minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-al-azma">Yusuf al-Azma</a> was killed. Faisal was expelled and became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> in 1921.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/arab-kingdom-of-syria.jpg" alt="Arab Kingdom of Syria" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Ch1902 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kingdom_of_Syria_(1920-03-08_to_1920-07-24).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Damascus</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Faisal I, Hashim al-Atassi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a>, <a href="/countries/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, <a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a>, <a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a>, <a href="/countries/palestine">Palestine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Syria (1920), Syrian Arab Kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=arab-kingdom-of-syria" aria-label="Arab Kingdom of Syria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5607 962 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Arab Kingdom of Syria lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5927 1218L5709 970M5927 1218L5905 1205M5927 1218L6070 1642"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5905 1205h0M6070 1642h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5927 1218h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5927 1218h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Damascus. <a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=arab-kingdom-of-syria">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
